&lt;p&gt;Scale’s Global Public Sector (GPS) team is growing quickly as we work to &lt;strong&gt;build reliable AI systems for governments around the world&lt;/strong&gt;. This is one of the most ambitious and high-impact problems of our time, and our go-to-market team sits at the front line of it - building relationships with government customers, shaping complex deals, and turning pipeline into deployed programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;GTM Business Operations Associate&lt;/strong&gt; to make our sales team run with more rigour, predictability and speed. Working closely with the Head of Commercial Strategy &amp;amp; Operations, you’ll lead on getting new sellers productive fast and giving deal teams hands-on support on bids, tenders and pricing, and act as a key partner in running our sales operations and advisor program. This role is ideal for a highly analytical, commercially minded generalist - someone who thrives with autonomy and enjoys being close to deals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales enablement &amp;amp; GTM onboarding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and run onboarding for new GTM hires - building the curriculum, materials and 30/60/90-day milestones that get sellers productive quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain a central library of enablement content (product and use-case overviews, customer stories, competitive positioning, objection handling) and keep it current as our offerings evolve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, EPD and Marketing to turn new launches and capabilities into clear, field-ready training for the sales team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales operations - playbooks, process, tooling &amp;amp; forecasting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside the Head of Commercial Strategy &amp;amp; Operations to document and refine our sales playbooks, stage definitions, qualification criteria and deal handoffs, and support their rollout across regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep the GTM operating cadence running smoothly - weekly pipeline reviews, monthly forecast calls and quarterly business reviews - by preparing inputs, flagging risks and tracking follow-through on actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare the forecasting and pipeline reporting used by leadership, pulling together data from across the sales team and improving accuracy over time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep CRM (Salesforce) data clean and up to date, working with sellers on opportunity hygiene, and surface ideas for where tooling and AI could remove manual work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track GTM metrics (pipeline generation, conversion, win rates, cycle times, bookings vs. target) and turn the data into clear insights for the sales team and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Advisor program management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Head of Commercial Strategy &amp;amp; Operations on the day-to-day running of the advisor program - coordinating onboarding of new advisors and keeping a clear view of each advisor’s network, expertise and active engagements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate introductions, briefings and follow-ups between advisors and deal teams, so every engagement has a clear objective and next step&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track advisor impact (meetings sourced, pipeline influenced, deals supported) and prepare the analysis that informs where we invest, expand or refocus the program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Handle the operational side of advisor relationships, including agreements, check-in scheduling and internal reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deal support - bids, tenders &amp;amp; pricing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with deal teams on complex opportunities - helping structure pricing and commercial proposals, building pricing models, and coordinating internal approvals across finance, legal and leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the bid and tender process - tracking opportunities and deadlines, coordinating contributors across sales, EPD, legal and security, and keeping submissions on time and to a high standard&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a reusable bid library (standard responses, compliance and security answers, case studies, pricing templates) so each submission is faster and stronger than the last&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture learnings from wins and losses and feed them back into playbooks, pricing guidance and enablement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideally you would have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A penchant for digging deeply into the data yourself, thinking from first principles, and iterating quickly to deliver results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial instincts and a genuine interest in how deals get won - from first meeting to signed contract&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with CRM and reporting tools, and advanced Excel / Google Sheets and Claude skills; SQL or BI tools (e.g. Tableau, Looker) a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication - you can turn complex material into clear training content, crisp bid responses and polished executive-level comms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong project management skills, with the ability to run several workstreams and hard deadlines in parallel without dropping the ball&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong orientation toward outcomes, and a history of being scrappy when it counts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Low ego and highly collaborative - you’re excited to work alongside smart, humble teammates and do whatever it takes to help the team succeed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An easygoing interpersonal style that lets you hold sellers accountable on pipeline discipline while earning their trust, and build credibility with senior external advisors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build high-trust relationships with a wide range of people across sales, finance, legal and delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent qualitative and quantitative analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2-4 years in sales operations, revenue operations, sales enablement or business operations at a high-growth tech company, or at a top-tier VC firm, consulting firm, investment bank, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to enterprise or public sector sales cycles, including RFPs, tenders, frameworks or government procurement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building pricing, forecasting, capacity or territory planning models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting advisor, partner or channel programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
